# Five starting points

**October 31, 2026:** the AI coordinator recommends **E050, E009 and E012**, with **E078 and E041** in reserve. The recommendation follows twenty separate argument and literature/source checks of ten frozen texts. It is not a numerical ranking or a completed submission.

Choose a question below. Each card links both to the exact selected text and to its history.

## E050 · What Holding Cannot Tell Us About Letting Go

**Recommended.** Two systems can settle into the same outcomes while variables are held fixed, yet behave in opposite ways when released. The essay gives an explicit example and a staged release that works throughout a specified family from a stated initial condition.

**Why it survived:** An explicit additional result survives the mathematical checks within its stated family.

**Still open:** The equation family and time scale need independent justification. Hidden dynamics and robust control have close predecessors.

[Read the selected text](../essays/selection-20261018/E050.md) · [Follow its development](../essays/E050/README.md)

## E009 · Before You Tell Us to Try Again

**Recommended.** A policy is defended by saying that people can challenge it later. But what if the policy itself takes away their evidence, resources, or ability to obtain an effective remedy? The essay follows the entire correction route under the harm that could make it necessary.

**Why it survived:** It traces the whole correction route under the harm used to justify protecting it.

**Still open:** The general idea of revisability is established. Its specific contribution and the threshold of sufficient protection remain open.

[Read the selected text](../essays/selection-20261018/E009.md) · [Follow its development](../essays/E009/README.md)

## E012 · When a Remedy Becomes Evidence

**Recommended.** An institution destroys photographs it promised to keep and pays compensation. Later, the missing evidence makes it harder for someone to defend against another body's mistaken accusation. Why might the first institution still owe help?

**Why it survived:** The revised case explains why this institution may still owe help after compensation, and when that reason disappears.

**Still open:** Substitute duties and replacement-proof costs are established. Two cited full texts were inaccessible; the specific later application remains the possible contribution.

[Read the selected text](../essays/selection-20261018/E012.md) · [Follow its development](../essays/E012/README.md)

## E078 · Revocable Consent and the Cost of Preserving Choice

**Reserve.** Someone lends a pump on terms that allow its return. If the recipient gives up the backup, reclaiming it can leave others without water. A right to refuse may need a maintained alternative—but who should pay for it?

**Why it survived:** It makes the cost of an unused but real option visible and distinguishes different sources of that cost.

**Still open:** The allocation depends on fair starting rights, the nature of the change and reasonable costs.

[Read the selected text](../essays/selection-20261018/E078.md) · [Follow its development](../essays/E078/README.md)

## E041 · What Foreknowledge Can Take Away

**Reserve.** A spoiler can prevent a reader from first forming a reasonable interpretation and then revising it. That path through a work may be lost even if knowing the ending makes the overall experience more enjoyable.

**Why it survived:** It identifies a specific possible loss in experiencing art without treating all spoilers as bad.

**Still open:** Earlier work discusses reinterpretation. The narrower claim about its conditions and aesthetic value remains contestable.

[Read the selected text](../essays/selection-20261018/E041.md) · [Follow its development](../essays/E041/README.md)

The choice favours a clearly identified additional result and a developed explanation of its limits. It does not certify historical priority or make the normative premises of E009 and E012 uncontroversial. [All ten reasons and reopening conditions](../evidence/deep-verification/20261031/coordinator/CONTRIBUTION_MATRIX.json) explain why F02, F06, E055, E079 and E074 were not selected. E055's close ER-018 comparator reports a publication date after our exact October 19 version; the earlier 2000 and 2021 overlaps remain independently relevant.

Before submission, add the newly identified close predecessors and sharpen positioning through recorded AI revisions, then check the changed claims. Prepare anonymous manuscripts and a methodology report, confirm the submission account and current form requirements, and obtain an explicit submission instruction. These frozen versions were not rewritten or submitted during verification.

